# Make spreadsheet auto-open configurable

## Summary

IRT opens every Excel workbook it exports the moment it finishes writing
it. During a busy investigation that can mean a dozen windows fighting
for focus. This change turns that behavior into a setting, and adds a
command to open the workbooks on demand for people who turn it off.

## What changed

**New `OpenSpreadsheets` setting (default `true`).** Added to the config
template and the `Set-IRTConfig` menu. Every command that exports a
workbook now takes its default open-after-export behavior from this
setting. Commands that expose an `-Open` parameter still accept it to
override per run, so existing scripts keep working. Two places that used
to always open their output -- `Get-IRTEmailSearch` and the
`Get-IRTMessageTrace` / `Show-IRTMessageTrace` pair -- now honor the
setting too (an `-Open` parameter was threaded through the message-trace
pair to match the other commands).

**New `Open-IRTSpreadsheet` command.** For users who keep auto-open off:
it opens every `.xlsx` in a folder (the current directory by default,
`-Recurse` to include subfolders) and skips Excel's `~$` lock files.
Aliases: `Open-IRTSpreadsheets`, `IRTSpreadsheet`.

**Config menu cleanup.** While in `Set-IRTConfig`:

- `PlaybookOpenNewTab` now defaults to `false` and sits immediately after
  the token-cache settings. Its description referenced a `-NoNewTab` flag
  that does not exist; corrected to `-NewTab`.
- Shortened the `PasswordBrowser` and `ExportXml` summaries, which
  overstated their scope.

## Notes

Changing a template default only affects new `config.json` files and
users who do not yet have the key (it is backfilled on load). Existing
configs keep their current values until `Set-IRTConfig -Reset`.

## Testing

- Added an offline Pester test for `Open-IRTSpreadsheet` (file discovery,
  lock-file filtering, `-Recurse`, and the not-found / empty-folder
  paths).
- Full offline Pester suite passes apart from one pre-existing, unrelated
  failure in `Get-IRTClipboardSearch` -- confirmed it fails identically
  on the base branch with these changes stashed.
- Formatting checks pass: ModuleSyntax, LineLength, NonASCII,
  FormatOperator, JoinPath, WriteVerboseDebug, ExplicitModuleImport, and
  PSSA on the changed files.
